  "grip_rationale": "The far gripping hand is drawn at skin Cells (7,11) and (8,12) where the haft diagonal crosses the chest. grip is pinned to anchor Cell (8,11) at the haft contact on the bridging leather Cell between those skin Cells.",
  "assignment_rationale": "Non-outline core Cells are classified from polished material roles and anchor-space regions aligned with identity-lock rectangles. hand_near is the visible near hand: skin Cells (5,12) and (5,13) plus outline and leather Cells that 4-connect to them. hand_far is the drawn far grip: skin Cells (7,11) and (8,12) plus bridging Cell (8,11). tool_handle is an authored trace along the Master Palette darkest amber #783A18 run (4,7) (5,8) (6,8) (8,8) (8,10) and the Cells that 4-connect it from tool_head to hand_far across the y9-10 gap; (8,8) is cheek light but keeps the haft one component. The x6..8 y9..14 chest mass is beard ramp, not sleeve. arm_near is green-cloth sleeve at x<=6 only. belt is the kinematic root verified by the buckle landmark. Anchor Cells (14,16)..(15,17) stay with beard or legs for connectivity. Cell (12,5) is in lamp. Stone Cells (11,2) and (11,3) remain in helmet as the lantern mounting bracket. Issue #300 re-roles tool haft to stone and glove leather to skin in identity-roles.json so material roles align with tool and hand parts. The y14 row is the beard's dark bottom fringe passing behind both gloves: outline Cells (6,14) and (8,14) stay with beard so the fringe remains one connected edge and both gloves stay pure-skin footprints.",
